  "scope": "For each finite initial essential stock at least five, an explicit positive seed interval fails within a finite horizon under every time-varying beta and quality error schedule and every nonnegative stock shock. The inherited share growth and support laws stay fixed; there is no direct entry or stock injection. The same positive seed has projected finite recovery under the original zero-beta pulse while its full guarded history terminates. Not an exact viability kernel, a physical extinction theorem, or a zero-substantive-axiom foundation."
}
